{"id":"payees-at-homes-planning-check","title":"Payees registered at a home or an empty lot: a second land-use record","question":"When the assessor classes a large payee's only registered address as a home or vacant land, does Planning's land-use file agree?","finding":"59 payees paid $1 million or more are registered only on parcels the assessor classes as homes or vacant land (the places screen's test, re-run on the 23 November address file). Planning's land-use file disagrees for 19 of them: it records commercial space or homes on the parcel, or the class is a live/work unit (Bar Association of San Francisco, 936 Geary LP, Accend Networks, Mission Asset Fund, Transbay 2 Senior L.P., Aramark Correctional Services LLC and others). For 31 both records show housing only, 10 of them confirmed by a contract notice or directory address: a firm run from a home, which is ordinary.","how":"The places screen joined a payee to its registry account by name, the address to a parcel and the parcel to the assessor's class. Here the address is re-placed with the Enterprise Addressing System file of 23 November 2026, the class code is decoded with the Assessor-Recorder's class-code table, and Planning's land-use file adds the number of homes and the square feet of commercial uses on the same parcel. Parcels are tested against the former Redevelopment Agency project areas.","limits":"Planning's land-use file is a snapshot of building use, not of who works there. A registration address is where the tax bill goes. \"Vacant\" in the roll covers land under construction and public land, and several rows are housing partnerships or a public building's contractor. The payee-to-registry join is a name match unless the last column says otherwise. Homes are never printed.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"payee","t":"City payee","type":"org"},{"k":"paid","t":"Paid since fiscal 2019","type":"usd"},{"k":"dept","t":"Mostly from","type":"text"},{"k":"assessor","t":"Assessor class","type":"text"},{"k":"planning","t":"Planning land use","type":"text"},{"k":"redevelopment","t":"Former redevelopment area","type":"text"},{"k":"neighborhood","t":"Neighborhood","type":"text"},{"k":"basis","t":"How the payee and the registration were joined","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"payee":"Bar Association of San Francisco","paid":18261712,"dept":"Mayor","assessor":"Vacant Street Parcel","planning":"Planning records 6,114 sq ft of commercial space","redevelopment":"-","neighborhood":"Financial District/South Beach","basis":"same street address on its City contract notice or directory entry"},{"payee":"936 Geary LP","paid":11600000,"dept":"Mayor","assessor":"Apartment 4 units or less","planning":"Planning records 10,477 sq ft of commercial space and 30 homes","redevelopment":"Bayview Hunters Point Area B Zone 2 (plan ends 2036)","neighborhood":"Bayview Hunters Point","basis":"same street address on its City contract notice or directory entry"},{"payee":"Accend Networks","paid":9955812,"dept":"Public Utilities Commsn","assessor":"Live/Work Condominium","planning":"live/work unit: zoned for work as well as living","redevelopment":"-","neighborhood":"South of Market","basis":"same street address on its City contract notice or directory entry"},{"payee":"Mission Asset Fund","paid":2575491,"dept":"GSA - City Administrator","assessor":"Apartment 4 units or less","planning":"Planning records 11,404 sq ft of commercial space and 6 homes","redevelopment":"-","neighborhood":"Bernal Heights","basis":"same street address on its City contract notice or directory entry"},{"payee":"Health Net","paid":52386681,"dept":"Health Service System","assessor":"Condominium","planning":"no Planning land-use record","redevelopment":"Western Addition A-2 (Expired) (plan ends 2009)","neighborhood":"Western Addition","basis":"name match only"},{"payee":"Transbay 2 Senior L.P.","paid":40986468,"dept":"Commty Invest & Infrstrctr","assessor":"Vacant Lot Gov","planning":"Planning records 335 homes on the \"vacant\" parcel","redevelopment":"Transbay Zone 1 (plan ends 2035)","neighborhood":"Financial District/South Beach","basis":"name match only"},{"payee":"Aramark Correctional Services LLC","paid":30711389,"dept":"Sheriff","assessor":"Vacant Lot Public Use","planning":"Planning records 1,330,482 sq ft of commercial space","redevelopment":"-","neighborhood":"South of Market","basis":"name match only"},{"payee":"Mission Bay 9 LP","paid":30184743,"dept":"Commty Invest & Infrstrctr","assessor":"Vacant land- residential 15+ units","planning":"no Planning land-use record","redevelopment":"Mission Bay - South (plan ends 2028)","neighborhood":"Mission Bay","basis":"name match only"},{"payee":"180 Jones Associates L.P.","paid":13950000,"dept":"Mayor","assessor":"Vacant land- residential 15+ units","planning":"Planning records 70 homes on the \"vacant\" parcel","redevelopment":"-","neighborhood":"Tenderloin","basis":"name match only"},{"payee":"T1 Partners","paid":11215067,"dept":"Airport Commission","assessor":"Vacant Street Parcel","planning":"Planning records 6,114 sq ft of commercial space","redevelopment":"-","neighborhood":"Financial District/South Beach","basis":"name match only"},{"payee":"30 Van Ness Development LLC","paid":10502708,"dept":"GSA - City Administrator","assessor":"Vacant land- residential 15+ units","planning":"Planning records 180,363 sq ft of commercial space","redevelopment":"-","neighborhood":"Tenderloin","basis":"name match only"},{"payee":"Casa Adelante Housing LLC","paid":9495516,"dept":"Mayor","assessor":"Vacant land- residential 15+ units","planning":"Planning records 18,345 sq ft of commercial space","redevelopment":"-","neighborhood":"Mission","basis":"name match only"},{"payee":"San Francisco Safe Inc.","paid":8465706,"dept":"Police","assessor":"Vacant Lot Public Use","planning":"Planning records 665,241 sq ft of commercial space","redevelopment":"-","neighborhood":"South of Market","basis":"name match only"},{"payee":"Randall Museum Friends","paid